---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About IMX"
  description="What ACM IMX is, its history as the evolution of EuroITV and ACM TVX, and where to find its proceedings and awards."
>
  <div class="container page prose">
    <h1>About IMX</h1>

    <h2>What IMX is</h2>
    <p>
      The ACM International Conference on Interactive Media Experiences (IMX) is the leading international
      forum for the presentation and discussion of research in all areas related to the architecture, design,
      implementation, application and evaluation of interactive and immersive user experiences, both online
      and broadcast.
    </p>

    <h2>History</h2>
    <p>
      IMX is the evolution of the EuroITV conference on interactive TV and of ACM TVX. Its incorporation
      under the ACM banner, sponsored by ACM SIGCHI in cooperation with ACM SIGMM and ACM SIGWEB, extended
      its international reach and significance.
    </p>
    <p>
      See <a href={url('history/')}>every past edition</a>, where it was held and its proceedings, or read
      more about <a href={site.imxHistoryUrl}>the evolution of IMX within the context of SIGCHI conferences</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Governance</h2>
    <p>
      IMX is an ACM SIGCHI conference, and defers to ACM SIGCHI for all policies and procedures. Conference
      organisers follow the <a href={site.sigchiPoliciesUrl}>SIGCHI policies</a> and the
      <a href={site.sigchiOrganizersUrl}>SIGCHI guides for organisers</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The IMX <a href={url('committee/')}>Steering Committee</a> is governed by its
      <a href={url('files/imx-sc-rules-and-procedures.pdf')}>Rules and Procedures (PDF)</a>, which set out the
      committee's aims, membership, roles and responsibilities, meetings, and decision procedures.
    </p>

    <h2>Proceedings and awards</h2>
    <p>
      The proceedings of all editions, including paper awards, are in the
      <a href={site.acmDlUrl}>ACM Digital Library</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Archive</h2>
    <p>
      Journal special issues and edited books associated with IMX and its predecessor conferences are listed in
      the <a href={url('archive/')}>Special Issues archive</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
